## Interface: 11509, 20506, 16001
## Title: Readycheck |cff33ff99Consumables|r
## Notes: The consumable bars - main, potions, weapon oils and trinkets - and the raid consumables checker.
## Author: Zac
## Version: 1.0
## Dependencies: Readycheck, Readycheck_Features
## LoadOnDemand: 1
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Potion_41

# Two layers, kept in one addon so they switch off as a unit:
#   Checker      the raid consumables window and its popups
#   Consumables  the four bars (main, potions, weapons, trinkets) and the
#                shared button/cooldown/refresh machinery behind them
#
# ALL SETTINGS STAY IN ReadycheckDB (consumablesHelper, potionsBar,
# weaponsBar, trinketBar, consumablesChecker). They belong to the main
# addon on purpose: switching this off must not throw a setting away.
#
# What stays in the main addon, and why:
#   Systems\TTSEngine.lua      the speech engine used to live here as
#                              Consumables_TTS.lua. The reminder stack
#                              speaks through it too - RR_Engine alone has
#                              13 call sites - so announcements must not
#                              fall silent because the bars are off.
#   UI\Consumables\Cons_Base   publishes RC._sbc, the shared sidebar
#                              helpers that the bar pages here, the boss
#                              notes page and the reminder pages all read.
#   Core\Core_Stubs.lua        no-op fallback for every bar refresh method
#                              that core calls unguarded.
#
# RC._chInit is the ordered queue of init closures every file below
# appends to; Consumables_Bootstrap drains it once RC.db exists and so
# must stay last in its group.

# ---------- Consumables checker ----------
# Base defines RC.consumablesChecker and the icon cache the rest read.
# Bootstrap wires the events and loads last in this group.
Checker_Base.lua
# Must-have items: big on-screen icons when one is missing
Checker_Essentials.lua
Checker_Popup.lua
Checker_Render.lua
Checker_Window.lua
Checker_Bootstrap.lua

# ---------- The bars ----------
# Base is bar chrome only and creates RC._chInit, so it loads first.
# State defines RC.consumablesHelper / potionsBar / weaponsBar /
# trinketBar, which every file after it reads.
# Events is the one event frame the four bars share; it must come before
# any file that registers with it.
Consumables_Base.lua
# Style: the button look (fonts, colours, glow, entrance/exit) the bars
# and the settings previews share.
Consumables_Style.lua
Consumables_State.lua
Consumables_Events.lua
Consumables_Items.lua
Consumables_Buttons.lua
Consumables_Frames.lua
Consumables_Refresh.lua
Consumables_Weapons.lua
Consumables_Trinkets.lua
Consumables_Runtime.lua
Consumables_Bootstrap.lua

# ---------- UI, last ----------
# Sidebar pages; they read the tables built above and RC._sbc from the
# main addon.
# Shared Look/Text/Animation/Position tabs and the pane preview for the
# bar pages below; must load before them.
UI\Cons_BarStyle.lua
UI\Cons_Checker.lua
UI\Cons_HelperCfg.lua
UI\Cons_PotionsCfg.lua
UI\Cons_WeaponsCfg.lua
UI\Cons_TrinketCfg.lua
UI\Cons_Items.lua
